          "text": "Foot symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports feet are the same as always, with itch and scale on the soles and between the toes, worse in heat. No pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Foot examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Fine moccasin-type scale on soles with mild erythema. Interdigital maceration and scale between the 3rd–4th and 4th–5th toes bilaterally; no fissures, increased warmth, cellulitis, or ulcers. Mild malodour."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
